V82 HYPOTHESIS: replace contiguous equal-count syntax chunks with atomic dynamic
per-manifest claims. Each thread owns indexed local results, original-order
gather precedes sequential source/config/Context semantics. 2-4 scoped workers,
fresh bytes, no per-edge logs, no result mutex, no new dependencies or caches.
Every started handle explicitly joined before spawn/panic fallback. Ordinary
parse errors remain ordered values. No panic-abort recovery promised.

Exact original v81 public factor contract retained: process-cached opt-in only
RA_JIT_PARALLEL_MANIFEST_PARSE=1, all other values OFF. Fixed actual-batch raw
stderr line plus newline at most once/process, no dynamic counts:
ra-jit: parallel-manifest-parse-v81 batch
Only emitted after a real bounded batch completes, no eligibility-only marker.
ROOT must use a distinct v82 executable hash/source identity and prove activation
with its native fixtures/runtime. No phase/cache/performance inference from marker.

